   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q1: Basic NumPy Operations\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a program to create a NumPy 1D-array with 5 elements and perform basic operations like:\n",
    "- Addition of 2 in all elements\n",
    "- Multiply 3 with all elements\n",
    "- Divide every element by 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### a) Addition of 2 in all elements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "array = np.array([6, 10, 14, 16, 20])\n",
    "print(\"Original Array:\", array)\n",
    "print(\"After Adding 2:\", array + 2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### b) Multiply 3 with all elements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"After Multiplying by 3:\", array * 3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### c) Divide every element by 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"After Dividing by 2:\", array / 2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Q2: Array Manipulation\n",
    "\n",
    "### a) Reverse the NumPy array: arr = np.array([1, 2, 3, 6, 4, 5])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "arr = np.array([1, 2, 3, 6, 4, 5])\n",
    "print(\"Original Array:\", arr)\n",
    "reversed_arr = arr[::-1]\n",
    "print(\"Reversed Array:\", reversed_arr)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### b) Find the most frequent value and their indices\n",
    "#### i) x = np.array([1,2,3,4,5,1,2,1,1,1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1])\n",
    "print(\"Array x:\", x)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find unique values and their counts\n",
    "unique_x, counts_x = np.unique(x, return_counts=True)\n",
    "print(\"Unique values:\", unique_x)\n",
    "print(\"Counts:\", counts_x)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find most frequent element\n",
    "most_frequent_x = unique_x[np.argmax(counts_x)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMax occurrence is of: {most_frequent_x}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Frequency: {np.max(counts_x)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find indices of most frequent element\n",
    "indices_x = np.where(x == most_frequent_x)[0]\n",
    "print(f\"Indices: {indices_x}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### ii) y = np.array([1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 2, 4, 3, 3])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y = np.array([1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 2, 4, 3, 3])\n",
    "print(\"Array y:\", y)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find unique values and their counts\n",
    "unique_y, counts_y = np.unique(y, return_counts=True)\n",
    "print(\"Unique values:\", unique_y)\n",
    "print(\"Counts:\", counts_y)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find most frequent element\n",
    "most_frequent_y = unique_y[np.argmax(counts_y)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMax occurrence is of: {most_frequent_y}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Frequency: {np.max(counts_y)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find indices of most frequent element\n",
    "indices_y = np.where(y == most_frequent_y)[0]\n",
    "print(f\"Indices: {indices_y}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Q3: 2D Array Indexing\n",
    "\n",
    "For the given 2-D array arr = np.array([[10, 20, 30], [40, 50, 60], [70, 80, 90]]), access elements using row and column indices:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "arr3 = np.array([[10, 20, 30],\n",
    "                 [40, 50, 60],\n",
    "                 [70, 80, 90]])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"2D Array:\")\n",
    "print(arr3)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# a) Access 1st row, 2nd column (index [0,1])\n",
    "print(\"a) Access 1st Row, 2nd Column [0,1]:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Value: {arr3[0, 1]}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# b) Access 3rd row, 1st column (index [2,0])\n",
    "print(\"b) Access 3rd Row, 1st Column [2,0]:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Value: {arr3[2, 0]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Q4: Array Properties and Transpose\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a 1-D NumPy array named AnhadKohli with evenly spaced 25 numbers from 10 to 100 using linspace().\n",
    "\n",
    "Print:\n",
    "- Dimensions of the array\n",
    "- Shape\n",
    "- Total elements\n",
    "- Data type of each element\n",
    "- Total number of bytes consumed\n",
    "- Transpose using reshape()\n",
    "- Transpose using T attribute"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create array with 25 evenly spaced values from 10 to 100\n",
    "AnhadKohli = np.linspace(10, 100, 25)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Array Name: AnhadKohli\")\n",
    "print(\"Array Values:\")\n",
    "print(AnhadKohli)\n",
    "print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Array Properties"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Array Properties:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Dimension (ndim)     : {AnhadKohli.ndim}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shape                : {AnhadKohli.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total Elements       : {AnhadKohli.size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Data Type            : {AnhadKohli.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total Bytes (nbytes) : {AnhadKohli.nbytes}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Transpose using reshape()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nTranspose using reshape(25,1):\")\n",
    "transposed_reshape = AnhadKohli.reshape(25, 1)\n",
    "print(transposed_reshape)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape after reshape: {transposed_reshape.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Transpose using T attribute"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nTranspose using T attribute:\")\n",
    "transposed_T = AnhadKohli.T\n",
    "print(transposed_T)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape after T: {transposed_T.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nNOTE:\")\n",
    "print(\"For 1D arrays:\")\n",
    "print(\"  - .T has no effect (shape remains (25,))\")\n",
    "print(\"  - reshape() converts 1D to 2D column vector\")\n",
    "print(\"  - .T is most useful for 2D or higher-dimensional arrays\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Q5: Array Statistics and Reshaping\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a 2-D Array named ucs420_AnhadKohli with following values – 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90, 15, 20, 35.\n",
    "\n",
    "Compute:\n",
    "- Mean\n",
    "- Median\n",
    "- Max\n",
    "- Min\n",
    "- Unique elements\n",
    "\n",
    "Also:\n",
    "- Reshape to 4 rows × 3 columns → reshaped_ucs420_AnhadKohli\n",
    "- Resize to 2 rows × 3 columns → resized_ucs420_AnhadKohli"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create array with 12 elements\n",
    "ucs420_AnhadKohli = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90, 15, 20, 35])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Array Name: ucs420_AnhadKohli\")\n",
    "print(\"Original Array:\")\n",
    "print(ucs420_AnhadKohli)\n",
    "print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Array Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean               : {np.mean(ucs420_AnhadKohli)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Median             : {np.median(ucs420_AnhadKohli)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max                : {np.max(ucs420_AnhadKohli)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min                : {np.min(ucs420_AnhadKohli)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unique Elements    : {np.unique(ucs420_AnhadKohli)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reshape to 4 rows × 3 columns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nReshape to 4 rows × 3 columns:\")\n",
    "print(\"Name: reshaped_ucs420_AnhadKohli\")\n",
    "reshaped_ucs420_AnhadKohli = ucs420_AnhadKohli.reshape(4, 3)\n",
    "print(reshaped_ucs420_AnhadKohli)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {reshaped_ucs420_AnhadKohli.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Resize to 2 rows × 3 columns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nResize to 2 rows × 3 columns:\")\n",
    "print(\"Name: resized_ucs420_AnhadKohli\")\n",
    "resized_ucs420_AnhadKohli = np.resize(ucs420_AnhadKohli, (2, 3))\n",
    "print(resized_ucs420_AnhadKohli)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {resized_ucs420_AnhadKohli.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Important Difference: reshape() vs resize()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN reshape() AND resize():\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nreshape():\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Reshapes array without changing data\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Total elements must remain the same\")\n",
    "print(\"  - 12 elements → can reshape to (4,3), (3,4), (2,6), (6,2), (12,1), (1,12)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"resize():\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Resizes to new dimensions\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Truncates if new size < original size\")\n",
    "print(\"  - Repeats elements if new size > original size\")\n",
    "print(\"  - 12 elements → resize to (2,3) keeps only first 6 elements\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary of Key NumPy Operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"KEY NUMPY OPERATIONS COVERED:\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"1. Vectorization:        Operations apply to all elements\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: array + 2\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"2. Array Slicing:        Extract array subset\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: arr[2:5], arr[::-1]\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"3. 2D Indexing:          Access specific element in 2D array\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: arr[0,1]\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"4. linspace():           Create evenly spaced values\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: np.linspace(10, 100, 25)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"5. unique():             Find unique values and counts\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: np.unique(arr, return_counts=True)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"6. reshape():            Change dimensions without data loss\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: arr.reshape(4,3)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"7. resize():             Resize array to new dimensions\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: np.resize(arr, (2,3))\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"8. Statistics:           mean, median, max, min, std, var\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: np.mean(arr)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"9. Array Properties:     ndim, shape, size, dtype, nbytes\")\n",
    "print(\"   Example: arr.ndim, arr.shape\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"10. Transpose:           T attribute or reshape()\")\n",
    "print(\"    Example: arr.T or arr.reshape(25,1)\")"
   ]
  },
 
